# Client-facing chat carve-out

Extends BASE §1 *Client and analyst bodies*; its scope list also covers evidence plans (`agentctl plan resolve <TASK-ID> --kind evidence`).

Evidence comments carry no TBD or a/b/c lists. In a question body, a bare "Assumption (not decided)" line is not an answer path: name the default when silence decides it, and say outright when a question needs no analyst decision. See `~/.agents/kb/_shared/How-to-write-analyst-questions-with-options.md`.

Commit messages: light compression only, 1–2 concise sentences in the repo's style, not telegram-speak or caveman fragments. This does **not** authorize stock Caveman full/ultra as a session default. Code blocks and commands are never stylistically compressed.
